'''Ishmael Larry “Ish” Smith''' (born July 5, 1988) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player who is a professional scout for the [[Washington Wizards]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He played [[college basketball]] for the [[Wake Forest Demon Deacons men's basketball|Wake Forest Demon Deacons]]. Smith holds the record of playing for the most NBA franchises, at 13. He won an [[List of NBA champions|NBA championship]] with the [[Denver Nuggets]] in 2023.<ref>{{Cite web |title=DENVER NUGGETS WIN FIRST NBA CHAMPIONSHIP IN FRANCHISE HISTORY WITH 4-1 FINALS WIN OVER HEAT |url=https://www.nba.com/nuggets/news/denver-nuggets-win-first-nba-championship-in-franchise-history-with-4-1-finals-win-over-heat |access-date=2024-06-22 |website=www.nba.com |language=en}}</ref>

