'''Immanuel Jaylen Quickley''' (born June 17, 1999) is an American professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Toronto Raptors]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He played [[college basketball]] for the [[Kentucky Wildcats men's basketball|Kentucky Wildcats]] and was selected by the [[Oklahoma City Thunder]] in the first round of the [[2020 NBA draft]], but was traded to the [[New York Knicks]] before the start of his rookie season. After nearly four seasons with New York, Quickley was traded to the Raptors in 2023 as part of a package which sent forward [[OG Anunoby]] to the Knicks, making him become the starting [[point guard]] for Toronto.
